explanation: Embedded development is constrained by target hardware, memory, power, and timing. Datasheets and reference manuals define registers, electrical limits, clocking, and peripheral behavior; a development board abstraction does not remove those constraints.
codeExample: 
objective: Identify memory regions and peripheral blocks
objective: Find reset, clock, and interrupt information in a datasheet
objective: Explain polling versus interrupt-driven work
pitfall: Assuming register behavior from a different MCU family
