=== TOPIC ===
id: emb-power-security
title: Power, Secure Boot, and Device Lifecycle
roadmapId: embedded-systems-engineer
type: standard
targetSubroadmap: 
difficulty: Advanced
estimatedMinutes: 55
summary: Account for energy budgets, firmware authenticity, update safety, and long device lifetimes.
explanation: Power profiling should measure representative duty cycles. Secure boot verifies software authenticity during startup, while secure update design must handle interrupted updates, rollback policy, key management, and recovery. Threat models vary with physical access and device deployment context.
codeExample: 
objective: Measure power across realistic operating modes
objective: Describe secure boot and signed-update goals
objective: Plan recovery for failed firmware updates
pitfall: Storing signing keys in firmware images
pitfall: Designing updates without an interruption-safe recovery plan
