explanation: Backend systems receive untrusted requests, coordinate application logic and persistent state, and must remain correct under concurrency, partial failure, and operational change. Transactions and Concurrency Control covers aCID, isolation anomalies, locks, MVCC, optimistic concurrency and transaction boundaries. Work through the core mechanisms, the assumptions they rely on, and the trade-offs that affect correctness, maintainability, and performance. Connect the topic to the surrounding system rather than treating its terminology as an end in itself. Practice: Model a small application dataset, write representative queries or operations, and verify correctness under duplicate, missing, concurrent, and rollback scenarios.
