objective: Explain the purpose and operating model of transactions and concurrency control, including ACID, isolation anomalies, locks.
objective: Apply transactions and concurrency control to a representative implementation or analysis task, including MVCC, optimistic concurrency and transaction boundaries.
objective: Evaluate correctness, edge cases, limitations, and relevant complexity or operational trade-offs for transactions and concurrency control.
pitfall: Optimizing or changing schema without checking real query plans, transaction boundaries, data volume, and compatibility with existing readers/writers.
