objective: Explain the purpose and operating model of data access and nosql awareness, including Drivers/ORMs, query patterns, connection handling.
objective: Apply data access and nosql awareness to a representative implementation or analysis task, including document/key-value models and trade-offs.
objective: Evaluate correctness, edge cases, limitations, and relevant complexity or operational trade-offs for data access and nosql awareness.
pitfall: Optimizing or changing schema without checking real query plans, transaction boundaries, data volume, and compatibility with existing readers/writers.
prerequisites:
resource: CMU Database Systems|https://15445.courses.cs.cmu.edu/|course
