difficulty: Intermediate
estimatedMinutes: 70
summary: Work with filesystems, ownership, permissions, mounts and storage capacity on Linux hosts.
explanation: Understand paths, file metadata, users and groups, mode bits, ACLs, mount points, disk usage, inode exhaustion and basic storage troubleshooting. Practice safe permission changes and inspect mounted filesystems.
codeExample:
objective: Explain the underlying model and the terms used to describe it.
objective: Apply the technique in a small, realistic implementation or operational scenario.
objective: Diagnose a failure by collecting evidence and checking assumptions.
pitfall: Applying a command or pattern without understanding its effect on adjacent systems.
pitfall: Treating a successful local test as proof of production readiness.
prerequisites: devops-linux-shell
